From 33cf9fee95e21246bc4de50c365479dd86d508e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Koskovich <akoskovich@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 16 Apr 2026 22:41:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 043/144] net: ipa: add new QMI request for HW filter stats
 info
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Some IPA firmware versions on IPA 5.5 require ipa_filter_stats_info in
the init_modem_driver QMI request. For example on Eliza, if this is not
passed then shortly after IPA init the system will halt and reboot
shortly after.

Downstream this is marked as optional but does not seem to be the case
on newer IPA firmware versions.

Signed-off-by: Alexander Koskovich <akoskovich@pm.me>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-arm-msm/20260416-eliza-ipa-v1-3-f4109a8e43c4@pm.me/
[mrlund: keep shared v4.5–v5.5 fnr_idx_cnt at 0 so older platforms keep
the previous QMI layout; Eliza's non-zero count is in its private data]
Signed-off-by: Martin Lund <mrlund@hotmail.com>
Assisted-by: Grok Bot
(cherry picked from commit 3106212b584dace750863841cdc6669fb7a244b2)

Import-Patch: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm8750/dodge/patches/7.3/0061-net-ipa-add-new-QMI-request-for-HW-filter-stats-info.patch
Import-SHA256: c2d6d5163fd87c133749da76f1d0e9fc4abda6355af83ce9ebceff8992f8b535
